I disagree with that strategy.  Arrows are your emergency "everything
must die now" attack.  It is important to build up the bow skill
before you have max luck, because you need those extra shots per turn
in case stuff needs to die immediately.

Basically, I use daggers on most the stuff in the early game, and
switch to arrows for the stuff I don't want to melee.  And if it seems
like I'm not shooting enough arrows in the early game, then I'll use
the bow more just so I can boost the bow skill.  If you use the bow a
moderate amount, then you'll be able to use it in the early game, and
still have enough arrows for the rest of the game.


